                                                "sense_id": "c70646c0-f632-3314-af44-9f2566af19ae",
                                                "text": "Alton Park, near the sea, was the Park made by Richard de Belmeis, Bishop of London, and he enclosed with it the wood then belonging to the Canons of St. Paul, and called [it] \"Edulvesnase\"\"—so that there was evidently a \"nase\" or promontory on this spot."
